    "chunk_size_bytes": 1538,
    "chunk_text": "He added that the management continues to meet staff to improve and add facilities for them.\n\nFernando noted that the team is drawn almost entirely from the resort\u2019s immediate surroundings, describing the jobs as a source of income and professional standing for the community around Rathgama.\n\nFernando kept his own remarks brief, insisting that \u201cAditya is all about all of you, our staff, and our partners\u201d. He pledged to carry those relationships into the resort\u2019s third decade so that guests continue to leave with \u201ca memorable, beautiful experience\u201d.\n\nAditya\u2019s average occupancy stands at around 60 percent, Fernando told Mirror Business, rising to as much as 95 percent in the peak season, when the resort is at times fully booked. Across its 16 keys, that translates to roughly 10 suites taken on an average night, climbing to 15 and, on some nights, all 16 at the height of the season.\n\nThe resort stands on seven acres of land, of which 5.5 acres, close to four-fifths, can be developed. Fernando revealed that the company is exploring possibilities and weighing proposals for that space. How the land is eventually used will show whether the less-is-more thinking that shaped the original resort carries into its next chapter.\n\nFittingly for a resort that began as a holiday home planned by a group of friends, the anniversary unfolded less as a corporate function than as a reunion of the people who built it, staff it and keep returning to it. As Akbarally put it in his address, \u201cSo that\u2019s Aditya for you.\u201d"
