    "chunk_text": "\u2018What kind of thinking is this?\u2019 President questions pin-sticking protests\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake has questioned the thinking behind certain opposition groups resorting to unusual protest methods, including inserting pins into clay figures.\n\nAddressing the National Convention of the National Intellectuals Organization (NIO) on Saturday (31), the President said groups that had benefited from the previous political culture were struggling to accept the changes introduced by the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) government.\n\nHe accused these groups of responding to the government\u2019s reforms with hateful statements, fabricated claims and what he described as bizarre protest activities.\n\nReferring to the practice of inserting pins into clay figures, President Dissanayake questioned how anyone could believe that harming a clay figure would cause pain to another person.\n\nHe criticised such actions, questioning the mindset behind attempts to use these methods as a form of political protest."
