    "chunk_text": "Cyclone Arnab affects over 21,000 people\n\nColombo, Nov. 1 (Daily Mirror) - A total of 21,356 people from 5,800 families have been affected by adverse weather conditions and Cyclonic Storm \u2018Arnab\u2019 across Sri Lanka, the Disaster Management Centre (DMC) said.\n\nThe affected population was recorded between October 23 and November 1, 2026, with the disaster impacting 137 Divisional Secretariat Divisions in 19 districts.\n\nAccording to the DMC, six people have died and eight others have been injured due to the adverse weather conditions, while three people remain missing.\n\nThe weather-related incidents have also resulted in the complete destruction of eight houses, while another 737 houses have sustained partial damage.\n\nRatnapura District has recorded the highest number of affected people, with 10,051 individuals from 2,666 families impacted across 15 Divisional Secretariat Divisions."
