    "chunk_size_bytes": 1938,
    "chunk_text": "Indian opposition stage mega rally seeking election chief\u2019s resignation\n\nFRANCE 24 - India\u2019s opposition parties on Sunday renewed calls for the resignation of the country\u2019s election chief, staging fresh protests in the latest display of public dissent against Prime Minister Narendra Modi\u2019s government.\n\nThe protest, called by opposition bloc INDIA, drew thousands of demonstrators, some carrying musical instruments and waving various flags, as they chanted slogans against the policies of the central government. Several opposition parties of the alliance, formed in 2023 to unseat Modi, mobilized their cadres from different states for the protest, which comes weeks after a police crackdown on protesters in New Delhi.\n\nLed by Rahul Gandhi, leader of the main opposition Congress party, and backed by the youth \u201cCockroach\u201d movement, the protesters called for the safeguarding of India\u2019s democracy while demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar over a contentious voter roll revision.\n\nThe protesters gathered at Ramlila Maidan, a sprawling public square in New Delhi, after police last month withdrew Jantar Mantar from the list of officially designated venues for demonstrations. The historic observatory had long served as the capital\u2019s main protest site.\n\nAuthorities deployed thousands of police and paramilitary soldiers and mounted extensive surveillance, with more than 200 CCTV cameras, drones and body-worn cameras at the venue and along the protest route, officials said.\n\nThe ongoing review of voter lists has removed more than 130 million names since last year. Critics say the exercise is politically motivated, threatens to disenfranchise millions more, and has disproportionately affected minorities, particularly Muslims.\n\nThe Election Commission and Modi\u2019s administration deny the allegations and say the revision is intended to remove duplicate and ineligible entries."
