    "chunk_size_bytes": 1975,
    "chunk_text": "Kumar Sangakkara opens up on Ryanair \u2019race storm\u2019\n\nDaily Mail - Kumar Sangakkara has opened up on what he believes was the racist treatment he and his family received during an argument at check-in at Dublin airport after a member of Ryanair staff told them: \u2018You people with your kinds of passports should expect this.\u2019\n\nSangakkara, who scored 12,400 runs in a glittering 134-Test career with Sri Lanka, was preparing to fly back to Bristol following a two-day trip to celebrate his 49th birthday when he says he was spoken to rudely by a woman following confusion over an e-visa.\n\nHe says he went out of his way to make \u2018doubly sure\u2019 he was following the correct procedure with his family\u2019s Sri Lankan passports.\n\nBut despite being assured two hours earlier by staff at the visa check desk that he didn\u2019t need to reproduce the e-visas on his mobile phone at the boarding gate \u2013 a process that can take several minutes \u2013 and despite already clearing security, he was still told to step aside and download the e-visas after he arrived at the gate.\n\nSangakkara told Daily Mail Sport: \u2018I said to one of the lady\u2019s colleagues, \u201cI will do this, but it is a bit of a procedure.\u201d I also said: \u201cWe went to your visa desk just to avoid this confusion. They gave us one message, and it\u2019s a bit confusing to passengers. But give us time.\u201d\n\n\u2018As I was accessing the e-visa on the side, this lady from behind the desk raised her voice so the entire area could hear and said: \u201cHurry up! Hurry up! You have to do this quickly, otherwise I\u2019m going to close boarding. Hurry up and get this done. Step aside now.\u201d Sangakkara asked for more time to access the e-visas, only to be told once again to hurry up, at which point he told the lady she was being \u2018very rude\u2019.\n\nHe says she responded by saying he was being \u2018argumentative and aggressive\u2019, adding: \u2018I\u2019m going to treat you as a threat to other passengers on board and not board you.\u2019"
  },
