    "md5": "163ab2e91a06d50484f6955ce7714559",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1034,
    "chunk_text": "Was \u2018Lankeswara\u2019 shot dead? Elephant killed, tusk reportedly removed in Kahatagasdigiliya\n\nColombo, Nov. 1 (Daliy Mirror) - Another elephant has reportedly been shot dead in a forest reserve in the Kahatagasdigiliya area of Anuradhapura, raising fresh concerns over the killing of elephants in the country.\n\nThe incident is believed to have taken place around two days ago, with reports suggesting that one of the elephant\u2019s tusks had been removed after it was killed.\n\nResidents in the area suspect that the elephant could be the tusker known as \u2018Lankeswara\u2019, although its identity has not yet been officially confirmed.\n\nThe elephant is reportedly not among the 13 elephants previously identified by the Government for special protection.\n\nThe suspected killing has raised questions about the safety of Sri Lanka\u2019s remaining tuskers and the effectiveness of measures introduced to protect elephants.\n\nAuthorities are yet to officially confirm the identity of the dead elephant or the circumstances surrounding its death."
