    "md5": "e80fe8b2cd6a04eea5fd82d5cfa06e56",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1756,
    "chunk_text": "TEDxColombo: Unlocking Fractured Paradox\n\nTEDxColombo, one of the most prominent and long-standing TEDx events in Sri Lanka, announced the 14th edition of its flagship event, scheduled for Sunday, November 29, 2026, at the iconic Temple Trees.\n\nKnown for pushing boundaries and sparking dialogue, TEDxColombo 2026 promises another unforgettable day of insight, inspiration and bold new ideas - brought to you by a carefully curated lineup of speakers that truly embody this year\u2019s theme - challenging the way we see the world, one \u2018mad\u2019 idea at a time.\n\nSince its inception in 2009, TEDxColombo has remained dedicated to spotlighting powerful local voices and homegrown stories that resonate far beyond our shores. The talks from the previous editions have reached global audiences through the TED platform, sparking meaningful conversations and even shifting perspectives in communities around the world. In its 16th year, TEDxColombo invites us all to look at the world through a different lens. Under this year\u2019s theme, \u2018The Fractured Paradox\u2019, explores how, with today\u2019s world doused heavily under the questioning gaze of what\u2019s real and what isn\u2019t, artificial intelligence becomes mankind\u2019s technological corn syrup, making it inevitable that fractures are everywhere. In our personal lives. In our communities. In the systems we trust. In the identities we carry. Yet, within those fractures often lies growth, change, perspective and possibility.\n\nThrough a carefully curated selection of powerful speakers, change makers and transformative experiences, TEDxColombo 2026 aims to challenge assumptions, as always, spark dialogue and take it a step further into reality, reminding us that even in contrast, there can be connection."
  },
