    "chunk_size_bytes": 1652,
    "chunk_text": "Tisara De Silva inducted as President of OPA for 2026/2027\n\nTisara De Silva was inducted as President of the Organisation of Professional Associations of Sri Lanka (OPA) for the term 2026 to 2027 at 51st organisation\u2019s Annual General Meeting held on 30 October 2026.\n\nHis elevation to the Presidency marks a significant milestone for the Pharmaceutical Society of Sri Lanka (PSSL), as he becomes the first professional from (PSSL)\n\nto assume the presidency of OPA which is founded in 1975, OPA serves as the apex body representing 52 Member Associations across 32 professions. Its role in bringing together diverse professional disciplines provides an important platform for collective engagement, policy dialogue and constructive contributions to national development.\n\nHis election as President-Elect of OPA in the preceding year, secured with a high majority of votes, reflected the confidence placed in his leadership and the esteem in which he is held within the professional community.\n\nDe Silva brings to the Presidency extensive institutional experience, professional insight and a longstanding commitment to organisational development. He served as General Secretary of OPA for two consecutive years, 2023-2024 and 2024-2025, and as Chairman of the Premises Maintenance Committee. In 2022- 2023 he served as Vice-President of OPA and Chairman of the Seminars, Workshops and Programs Committee. Further, his involvement in the Executive Council over many years and his 23-years experiences and association with the OPA General Forum reflect a sustained commitment to the organisation\u2019s governance, activities and wider professional mission."
  },
