    "chunk_text": "De Silva brings to the Presidency extensive institutional experience, professional insight and a longstanding commitment to organisational development. He served as General Secretary of OPA for two consecutive years, 2023-2024 and 2024-2025, and as Chairman of the Premises Maintenance Committee. In 2022- 2023 he served as Vice-President of OPA and Chairman of the Seminars, Workshops and Programs Committee. Further, his involvement in the Executive Council over many years and his 23-years experiences and association with the OPA General Forum reflect a sustained commitment to the organisation\u2019s governance, activities and wider professional mission.\n\nHis professional career spans more than 32 years in the Pharmaceutical Industry, including 27 years in senior management at GlaxoSmithKline Pharmaceuticals, a leading Multinational Pharmaceutical Company. This experience has provided him with extensive exposure to pharmaceutical operations, organisational management and leadership within an international corporate environment.\n\nHis academic and professional development includes a Master of Business Administration (MBA) from Malaysia, a Diploma in Modern Management from the United Kingdom, and a Diploma in Computer Programming. This combination of professional experience, management expertise and educational background has shaped his contributions to institutional leadership and the advancement of the pharmaceutical sector."
