    "chunk_text": "Group earnings before interest and taxes (EBIT) increased by 10.5% YoY to Rs. 6.1 billion, while the EBIT margin stood at 15.1%, compared to 17% in 1HFY26. Higher net finance income and a lower effective tax rate supported the Group\u2019s profitability, with the PAT margin improving to 9.2% from 8% in the previous year. The Group also recorded stronger second-quarter momentum, with revenue increasing by 32% YoY to Rs. 21.6 billion and PAT growing by 82.4% YoY to Rs. 2.3 billion.\n\nThe Group\u2019s Healthcare sector recorded revenue of Rs. 19.6 billion during 1HFY27, representing a 13.3% YoY increase. Growth accelerated during the second quarter, with revenue rising by 20.5% YoY. The sector\u2019s EBIT margin however, declined to 11.2% from 13.1% in 1HFY26, mainly due to regulated price reductions and the impact of a weaker rupee on imported products. The Pharmaceutical agency segment recorded a 24% YoY revenue contraction, mainly due to a change in operating model compared to last year, lower shipments from certain principals and regulatory-related stock shortages. Medical Devices and Healthguard Distribution recorded revenue growth of 19.9% and 4.1% YoY, respectively, while Healthguard Pharmacy remained broadly stable. Lina Manufacturing, the Group\u2019s pharmaceutical manufacturing arm, delivered a strong performance with revenue increasing by 35.1% YoY, supported by deliveries against government orders.\n\nDuring the period, Sunshine Holdings also advanced its commitment to strengthening local pharmaceutical manufacturing by finalising the joint venture agreement with India\u2019s Zydus Lifesciences Limited. The joint venture signed an agreement with the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI) to develop a GMP-compliant oral solid dosage manufacturing facility at the Horana Export Processing Zone."
  },
