    "chunk_size_bytes": 1843,
    "chunk_text": "During the period, Sunshine Holdings also advanced its commitment to strengthening local pharmaceutical manufacturing by finalising the joint venture agreement with India\u2019s Zydus Lifesciences Limited. The joint venture signed an agreement with the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI) to develop a GMP-compliant oral solid dosage manufacturing facility at the Horana Export Processing Zone.\n\nThe Group\u2019s Consumer sector delivered strong revenue growth of 53.5% YoY to Rs. 15 billion in 1HFY27, primarily driven by the consolidation of JAPC and the recovery of its tea export business. Excluding JAPC, sector revenue increased by 13% YoY, supported by growth in branded tea and tea exports. The sector\u2019s EBIT margin improved to 8.0% from 7.8% in the corresponding period last year.\n\nThe Branded Tea business recorded revenue growth of 5.6% YoY, led by Watawala Thei, while Zesta continued to operate in a highly competitive premium tea market. The Confectionery business registered a 2.2% YoY revenue increase, supported by growth in gums and wafers, which offset declines in toffee and candy categories.\n\nThe Tea Export business recorded a strong recovery, with revenue increasing by 25.4% YoY during 1HFY27. Second-quarter revenue grew by 60.9% YoY, driven by additional business from key customers and a higher contribution from value-added tea products.\n\nMeanwhile, JAPC\u2019s spice export revenue grew by 28.6%, supported by demand across its key product categories. The consolidation of JAPC further strengthened the Consumer sector\u2019s export portfolio, expanding the Group\u2019s presence in the spice export business.\n\nThe Group\u2019s Agribusiness sector, represented by Watawala Plantations PLC (CSE: WATA), recorded revenue of Rs. 5.6 billion during 1HFY27, reflecting a 7.2% YoY increase, primarily driven by the oil palm business."
