    "chunk_text": "They noted that while UN Human Rights Council (UNHRC) reports had called for the repeal of the Prevention of Terrorism Act (PTA), the Government was instead attempting to introduce alternative legislation that posed a significant threat to Tamils and the country as a whole. They also said the continued delay in holding Provincial Council elections had left their regions without a provincial administrative structure, which in turn facilitated land grabbing by State institutions.\n\nAccording to TELO, the High Commissioner responded that the need to hold Provincial Council elections had been highlighted in UNHRC reports. On the anti-terrorism legislation, he said the UK had closely monitored such proposals in the past, which had appeared in various guises, and remained deeply concerned about the current version, TELO said."
