    "chunk_size_bytes": 1921,
    "chunk_text": "\u2019Like a missile coming down\u2019 - Nine killed in fiery Florida jet crash\n\nBBC -A business jet crashed in a neighbourhood in Florida on Sunday, killing all nine people on board, the US transport secretary has said.\n\nThe crash happened near Cresthaven, some nine miles (14 km) from Mar-a-Lago, President Donald Trump's resort in the wealthy enclave of Palm Beach County, around 12:50 EST (17:50 GMT).\n\nImages from after the crash show a crater in the middle of a residential road, with patches of fire and pieces of concrete and debris from the Learjet 60 aircraft scattered.\n\nThe aircraft had departed from Austin, Texas, and was headed to the Bahamas, the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) said in a statement.\n\nUS media reports and flight analysis indicate that the jet was plummeting hundreds of feet per second before crashing.\n\nIn air traffic control audio recorded moments before the crash, the pilot of the aircraft can be heard saying the plane was descending 10,000 feet per minute, according to the BBC's US partner CBS News.\n\nThen the pilot declared an emergency, yelling, \"We are in an overspeed condition descending 20,000 feet per minute,\" CBS reported.\n\n\"We're gonna crash ... We're out of time,\" the pilot told the tower.\n\nUnverified footage posted on social media shows what appears to be a dash-camera recording of the moment of the crash. It shows vehicles driving on a residential suburban street, when suddenly an aircraft nosedives into the ground almost vertically, and explodes into a large fireball.\n\n\"When you see that video, it's a jarring thing,\" Florida Governor Ron DeSantis told reporters at a news conference after the crash. \"It's like a missile coming down, and a massive explosion, debris going everywhere.\"\n\nIt is not yet clear who was aboard the jet when it crashed. DeSantis said \"as of now, we don't have any reports of anyone who was on the ground...who was killed or injured\"."
  },
